se,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","number":16,"title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":5793,"closed_issues":0,"state":"open","created_at":"2022-07-26T12:42:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T14:39:14Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-10-10T21:19:14Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T20:59:52Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111492","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111492","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111492.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111492.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"- Inspired by [this](https://chat.godotengine.org/channel/core?msg=bkzkwAMpvLCKvvyB8) RC Thread\r\n\r\nImplements a new core template: `Enumerate`. This acts as a solution to the problem brought up in the above chat, where C++ lacks a native means of performing range loops with an index. At the time I brainstormed a wrapper workaround, but only now have found the time to construct that implementation. This format takes heavy inspiration from Python's `enumerate()`, which is where the name is lifted from:\r\n```cpp\r\n// Before:\r\nint index = 0;\r\nfor (something : array) {\r\n\t...\r\n\tif (condition) {\r\n\t\tcontinue; // Incrementing index erroneously skipped.\r\n\t}\r\n\t...\r\n\tindex++;\r\n}\r\n\r\n// Before (alt):\r\nint index = -1; // Start index one earlier.\r\nfor (something : array) {\r\n\tindex++; // Absolute first action taken, won't be skipped but declaration is unituitive.\r\n\t...\r\n}\r\n\r\n// After:\r\nint index = 0;\r\nfor (something : Enumerate(array, index)) {\r\n\t// No initial incrementation necessary.\r\n\t...\r\n\tif (condition) {\r\n\t\tcontinue; // Index will increment as expected!\r\n\t}\r\n\t...\r\n\t// No final incrementation necessary.\r\n}\r\n\r\n// After (C++20):\r\nfor (int index = 0; something : Enumerate(array, index)) {\r\n\t// Index and iterables entirely scoped to for-loop.\r\n}\r\n```","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111492/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":4,"eyes":3},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111492/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}